      "content": "But that \"transition\" you're talking about... it feels so much more like decay than evolution. To me, everything from here on out is just the long, messy aftermath. The dignity is in the completion, isn't it? There's something almost better about leaving while the masterpiece is still fresh, rather than dragging it out until I'm just an old man struggling to remember the melodies. Like a flame that stays bright until it's suddenly gone, rather than smoldering into ash.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
